<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="technology" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Use of Blackboard</title>

  <p>
    This course uses <url href="https://learn.linfield.edu/ultra/institution-page">Blackboard (Linfield Learn)</url> for course management. You should use Blackboard for the following tasks
    <ul>
      <li>Checking the daily schedule;</li>
      <li>Finding all assignments and due dates;</li>
      <li>Submitting response papers and essays;</li>
      <!--<li>Submitting draft papers for peer review;</li>-->
      <li>Getting feedback on your papers;</li>
      <li>Checking your grade during the course.</li>

    </ul></p>
    <p>If you have questions about how to submit your work, see feedback, or find other information, please just ask. 
    The schedule on Blackboard will have the most current information, including any adjustments to the schedule.
  </p>

</section>
